</surname><given-names>MR</given-names></name><name><surname>Bredehoeft</surname><given-names>SJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Campbell</surname><given-names>ML</given-names></name><name><surname>Heimer</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Joyner</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Lorentsen</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Remley</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Bullock</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Bumgarner</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Zakeriniasar</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Kirkland</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Melroy</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Millikin</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Lack of clinical significance of "enzyme-only" red cell alloantibodies</article-title><source>Transfusion</source><year>1993</year><volume>33</volume><fpage>284</fpage><lpage>293</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8480348</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B12"><label>12</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Garner</surname><given-names>SF</given-names></name><name><surname>Devenish</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Barber</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Contreras</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The importance of monitoring 'enzyme-only' red cell antibodies during pregnancy</article-title><source>Vox Sang</source><year>1991</year><volume>61</volume><fpage>219</fpage><lpage>220</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1807065</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B13"><label>13</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Judd</surname><given-names>WJ</given-names><